      "title": "Executive Director of Athletics & Recreation",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\n\nLocation: Dallas\n\nPosition Overview: The Executive Director of Athletics & Recreation provides strategic leadership, direction, and oversight for the University's intercollegiate athletics and recreation programs. The Executive Director is responsible for the overall administration, planning, fiscal management, compliance, personnel, facilities, and operations of the department. The Executive Director ensures that Athletics & Recreation supports the University's mission and educational priorities while promoting student success, student-athlete well-being, competitive excellence, institutional engagement, and a positive campus experience. The position oversees the University's NCAA Division III intercollegiate athletic program as well as recreational programs, facilities, and initiatives serving the broader University community. The Executive Director serves as a member of the President’s Advisory Council (PAC) and collaborates with the President and fellow PAC members in the development and implementation of University-wide organizational strategy. In this role, the Executive Director contributes to institutional planning, decision-making, and cross-divisional initiatives that advance the University’s mission and strategic priorities, while aligning Athletics & Recreation programs, resources, and operations with those objectives. Education: Master’s Degree from a four-year college or university.  Experience: Minimum of 5 years of progressively responsible and successful experience in collegiate athletic administration. Demonstrated experience supervising coaches, administrators, and/or professional staff. Previous successful experience in athletic administration at the college level. Previous coaching experience at the college level. Experience with NCAA Division III athletics strongly preferred. Knowledge and Skills: Thorough knowledge of NCAA Division III rules, regulations, compliance requirements, and best practices. Knowledge of the role of intercollegiate athletics and recreation within higher education and the student educational experience. Excellent interpersonal skills and outstanding organizational ability. Understanding of the role of athletics as an educational tool in the liberal arts environment. Thorough knowledge of “the business” of athletics. Ability to develop effective working relationships with senior leadership, faculty, staff, coaches, students, student-athletes, alumni, donors, families, and external partners. Proficiency with AI, internet and email, spreadsheet software, word processing software, and athletics, compliance, scheduling, financial, and other technology platforms as required. (Equivalent combinations of education, licenses, certifications and/or experience may be considered.) Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States. Misericordia University is not able to sponsor or transfer employment visas for this position.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=d687b185-ab48-45f0-afcf-5b1ceb8d32ea&ccId=9200921635429_3&jobId=9200990472902_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor | Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\n\nLocation: Dallas\n\nThe Physical Therapy Department at Misericordia University, located in Dallas, Pennsylvania, invites applications for a full-time, 10-month, on campus faculty position, beginning August 2027. Rank and status are negotiable and dependent upon the applicant’s experience and qualifications. Review of applications will begin on November 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled.  Position Responsibilities The successful candidate will: Teach courses within the Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) curriculum. Engage students through innovative teaching methodologies and evidence-based practice. Advise and mentor students in academic and professional development. Participate in scholarly activities, research, and service to the department, university, and profession. Assist with student recruitment, admissions activities, program assessment, and accreditation processes. Support clinical education initiatives and foster relationships with healthcare and community partners. Required Qualifications 1. Earned academic doctorate from an accredited institution (preferred), or DPT and clinical specialty certification 2. Current Physical Therapy license or eligible for Pennsylvania Physical Therapy licensure. 3. Minimum of three years of contemporary clinical experience in their specialty area 4. Teaching experience in higher education 5. Excellent communication skills, both oral and written. In its review of candidates, the department will prioritize candidates with expertise in musculoskeletal physical therapy.  Other areas of contemporary expertise also will be considered. Misericordia University, founded in 1924 by the Sisters of Mercy, is located adjacent to the Pocono Mountains region of Northeastern Pennsylvania, approximately 2 hours from New York City, and Philadelphia. The university's approach of combining a quality liberal arts education with professional preparation and service to others has resulted in its wide regional acclaim.  Misericordia has a long history of providing the community with health care and education practitioners who are compassionate, well educated, and able to deal with the challenging demands of health care and education in today’s society. The College of Health Sciences and Education offers bachelors, masters and doctoral degree programs, as well as certificate programs in specialized areas. Curricula in all Health Sciences and Education degree programs support the mission of Misericordia University and its core values of mercy, service, justice and hospitality. Applications should include: Cover letter addressing qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Contact information for three professional references upon request Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States. Misericordia University is not able to sponsor or transfer employment visas for this position.",
      "department": ""
    },
