      "title": "Adjunct | Social Work",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\n\nLocation: Dallas\n\nAbout the Role: The Adjunct Social Work faculty member plays a critical role in delivering high-quality education to students pursuing careers in social work. This position involves designing and teaching courses that integrate theoretical knowledge with practical application, preparing students to address complex social issues effectively. The role requires fostering an inclusive and engaging learning environment that supports diverse student populations and promotes critical thinking. Additionally, the adjunct faculty member collaborates with full-time faculty and participates in curriculum development to ensure academic rigor and relevance. Ultimately, this position contributes to the development of competent, ethical, and compassionate social work professionals who can make a positive impact in their communities. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in Social Work (MSW) from a Council on Social Work Education (CSWE) accredited program. Relevant professional experience in social work practice or related fields. Demonstrated ability to teach or facilitate adult learning in an academic or professional setting. Strong communication and interpersonal skills to effectively engage with students and colleagues. Eligibility to work in the United States. Responsibilities: Prepare and deliver course materials for undergraduate or graduate social work classes in accordance with the institution’s curriculum standards. Engage students through lectures, discussions, case studies, and experiential learning activities to enhance understanding of social work principles and practices. Assess student performance through assignments, exams, and projects, providing timely and constructive feedback to support academic growth. Maintain regular office hours to advise and mentor students, addressing their academic and professional development needs. Collaborate with department faculty to update course content, participate in faculty meetings, and contribute to program improvement initiatives. Skills: The required skills enable the adjunct faculty member to design and deliver comprehensive social work education that bridges theory and practice. Effective communication skills are essential for presenting complex concepts clearly and fostering meaningful classroom discussions. Interpersonal skills support mentoring students and collaborating with colleagues to enhance the academic program. Preferred skills such as proficiency with educational technology facilitate engaging online or hybrid course delivery, expanding access to learning. Additionally, cultural competency and inclusivity skills ensure that teaching practices meet the needs of a diverse student body, preparing graduates for socially responsible professional roles. About University: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States. Misericordia University is not able to sponsor or transfer employment visas for this position. Misericordia University, founded by the Sisters of Mercy in 1924, is a comprehensive institution offering bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degree programs. Located in Northeastern Pennsylvania near the Pocono Mountains, the university is approximately 2.5 hours from both New York City and Philadelphia. Misericordia is recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, professional preparation, and service to others, rooted in the values of the Sisters of Mercy.",
