      "title": "Adjunct | History",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\n\nLocation: Dallas\n\nAbout the Role: The Adjunct History Instructor plays a vital role in delivering high-quality education to undergraduate students by teaching courses in various historical periods and themes. This position focuses on fostering critical thinking, analytical skills, and a deep understanding of historical contexts among students. The instructor will design and implement engaging lesson plans, assess student performance, and provide constructive feedback to support academic growth. Collaboration with department faculty to align course content with program goals and participate in curriculum development is also essential. Ultimately, this role contributes to the academic mission by preparing students to appreciate the complexities of history and its relevance to contemporary issues. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in History or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Demonstrated knowledge of historical research methods and historiography. Experience teaching history at the college or university level. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Responsibilities: Prepare and deliver lectures and course materials for assigned history classes. Develop and grade assignments, exams, and other assessments to evaluate student learning. Provide timely and meaningful feedback to students to support their academic progress. Maintain regular office hours to offer additional support and guidance to students. Collaborate with department faculty on curriculum development and program improvement. Stay current with developments in the field of history and incorporate relevant research into teaching. Adhere to institutional policies and contribute to a positive learning environment. Skills: The required skills enable the instructor to effectively communicate complex historical concepts and foster an inclusive classroom environment that encourages student participation. Strong organizational skills