      "title": "Graduate Assistant | Ice Hockey",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\n\nLocation: Dallas\n\nAbout the Role: The Graduate Assistant for Ice Hockey plays a pivotal role in supporting the coaching staff and contributing to the overall success of the ice hockey program at the collegiate level. This position is designed to provide graduate students with hands-on experience in athletic coaching, team management, and sports administration while pursuing their advanced degree. The Graduate Assistant will assist in planning and conducting practices, analyzing game footage, and helping with player development to enhance team performance. Additionally, the role involves administrative duties such as coordinating travel, managing equipment, and supporting recruitment efforts. Ultimately, this position aims to develop the candidate’s professional skills in sports management and coaching within a competitive collegiate environment. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. Acceptance into a graduate program at the university offering the assistantship. Demonstrated knowledge of ice hockey rules, strategies, and training techniques. Strong organizational and communication skills. Ability to work flexible hours including evenings and weekends as required by the team schedule. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience playing or coaching ice hockey at the collegiate or club level. Experience with video analysis software and performance tracking tools. Background in sports science, kinesiology, or a related field. Familiarity with NCAA compliance and recruiting processes. Proven ability to work collaboratively within a team-oriented environment. Responsibilities: Assist the head coach and coaching staff in planning and conducting daily practices and training sessions. Analyze game and practice footage to provide feedback and strategic insights to players and coaches. Support player development through individualized training programs and performance monitoring. Manage logistical tasks including coordinating team travel, scheduling, and equipment maintenance. Contribute to recruiting efforts by evaluating prospective student-athletes and assisting with communication. Maintain compliance with NCAA regulations and university policies related to the athletic program. Participate in team meetings, video sessions, and other activities to support overall team strategy and cohesion. Skills: The required skills such as knowledge of ice hockey and strong communication are essential for effectively assisting coaches and interacting with players to foster development and team cohesion. Organizational skills are used daily to manage schedules, coordinate travel, and ensure smooth operation of team logistics. Preferred skills like experience with video analysis software enable the Graduate Assistant to provide detailed performance feedback and strategic insights that enhance player and team performance. Familiarity with NCAA regulations ensures that all activities comply with governing rules, maintaining the integrity of the program. Collaboration and interpersonal skills are critical for working closely with coaching staff, athletes, and administrative personnel to support the program’s goals. About Company: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States. Misericordia University is not able to sponsor or transfer employment visas for this position. Misericordia University, founded by the Sisters of Mercy in 1924, is a comprehensive institution offering bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degree programs. Located in Northeastern Pennsylvania near the Pocono Mountains, the university is approximately 2.5 hours from both New York City and Philadelphia. Misericordia is recognized for its commitment to academic excellence, professional preparation, and service to others, rooted in the values of the Sisters of Mercy.",
