      "title": "Dean of Students",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-29\n\nLocation: Dallas\n\nPosition Overview:   In collaboration with the VPMISL and AVP, the Dean of Students provides strategic leadership for the developmental and operational aspects of student life, emphasizing student well-being, community standards, and holistic development. This position will supervise several departments to ensure that programming, resources, and services facilitate student development and student success. As a member of Mission Integration and Student Life, the Dean of Students will support underrepresented student populations.  Education: Master's degree in College Student Personnel, Educational Leadership, Counseling, or related field required.   Experience: Seven to ten years of experience in increasingly responsible and professional roles related to student affairs  Experience with judicial affairs and disciplinary protocols Demonstrated crisis management skills  Knowledge and experience with student support in areas that report to the position such as Campus Life, Counseling Center and/or Health and Wellness preferred.   Prior supervisory experience Work-Related Knowledge Ability to manage multiple projects, manage crisis situations and utilize creative and timely problem-solving skills with flexibility for efficient resolution. Strong working knowledge and understanding of established professional codes of ethics and best practices for Student Affairs professionals. (Equivalent combinations of education, licenses, certifications and/or experience may be considered.)",
