      "title": "Groundskeeper | Landscape Crew Member",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-30\n\nLocation: Dallas\n\nPosition Summary: Misericordia University is seeking a dependable and motivated Landscape Crew Member / Professional to support the maintenance and appearance of campus grounds. This position focuses on lawn care, trimming, and light landscaping services while contributing to the overall safety, functionality, and aesthetics of the University’s outdoor environment. Essential Duties & Responsibilities: Perform routine lawn care including mowing, edging, trimming, and fertilizing. Assist with landscape maintenance such as planting, pruning, mulching, and weed removal. Safely operate hand tools, power tools, and small machinery used in grounds maintenance. Support basic tree care, including trimming, pruning, and monitoring tree health. Participate in snow removal operations during winter months to ensure safe campus access. Maintain cleanliness and organization of work areas and equipment. Follow all University safety protocols and report hazards or maintenance needs promptly. Qualifications & Requirements: Valid PA Drivers License High School Diploma or GED Basic mechanical aptitude and familiarity with landscaping tools and equipment. Experience in lawn care, landscape maintenance, gardening, or horticulture preferred. Ability to operate small and large machinery is required. Knowledge of landscaping practices including mowing, trimming, planting, and irrigation setup. Ability to work outdoors in varying weather conditions and perform physically demanding tasks. Strong work ethic, reliability, and ability to work both independently and as part of a team. Willingness to learn new skills related to landscaping and outdoor maintenance. Prior experience is preferred   Physical Requirements · Ability to lift up to 50 + lbs. · Ability to stand, walk, bend, and perform repetitive physical tasks for extended periods. · Ability to work in heat, cold, rain, and other outdoor conditions. Why Join Misericordia University? This position offers hands‑on experience in landscaping, horticulture, and outdoor maintenance while contributing to the beauty and functionality of a vibrant university campus. Team members in the Grounds Department play an essential role in creating a welcoming environment for the entire campus community. Misericordia University is a private educational institution that was founded in 1924. It is nestled in the Back Mountain Community of Dallas, Pennsylvania and sits on 130 plus acres. As an employee at Misericordia, you will enjoy a menu of fringe benefits designed to add personal convenience and work-life balance to your life, including a generous pension plan, tuition for you and your family, on-site gym, healthcare, dental, vision, and plenty of paid time off. Pay:  $17.00/Hour",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=d687b185-ab48-45f0-afcf-5b1ceb8d32ea&ccId=9200921635429_3&jobId=9200966982646_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor | Criminology / Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-24\n\nLocation: Dallas\n\nMisericordia University  invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Criminology/Criminal Justice position. The successful candidate will begin in August 2027, though a January 2027 start may be possible if circumstances permit.. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching, scholarship, and student mentorship. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate courses in both criminology and criminal justice, including courses such as Introduction to Criminology, Criminological Theory, and Quantitative Research Methods, as well as other courses that support the curriculum. The successful candidate will also have the opportunity to develop and teach elective courses that align with their professional expertise and research interests. Candidates should demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate education and the ability to engage students in a dynamic learning environment. Service to the department, university, and profession is expected, consistent with the responsibilities of a tenure-track faculty member. Qualifications Ph.D. in Criminology, Criminal Justice, Sociology, or a closely related field required by the time of appointment College or university teaching experience preferred Demonstrated commitment to effective teaching and student success Potential for scholarly achievement and professional engagement Ability to contribute to the growth and development of the Criminology program Please note: Misericordia University is unable to sponsor employment visas for this position. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of appointment and throughout the duration of employment. Commitment to Inclusive Excellence Misericordia University is committed to fostering an inclusive educational environment and values the contributions of individuals with diverse backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Candidates are encouraged to highlight experiences, leadership, teaching, scholarship, or service that have supported student success and contributed to an inclusive learning environment. About Misericordia University Founded in 1924 by the Sisters of Mercy, Misericordia University is located in Dallas, Pennsylvania, in the scenic Pocono Mountains region of Northeastern Pennsylvania, approximately two hours from both New York City and Philadelphia. The University's mission combines a strong liberal arts foundation with professional preparation, service leadership, and experiential learning, creating an educational experience that prepares students for meaningful careers and lives of purpose. Application Process Inquiries should be directed to Dr. Matthew Thornburg, email: mthornburg@misericordia.edu. Review of applications will begin October 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, applicants should submit the following materials online at www.misericordia.edu/hr under Faculty Opportunities: Letter of application Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of research agenda Teaching evaluations (if available) Two letters of reference",
      "department": ""
    },
