      "title": "Safety Officer | Shuttle",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-22\n\nLocation: Dallas\n\nPosition Title: Campus Shuttle Driver Department: [Transportation/Public Safety – adjust as needed] Status: Part-Time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Hourly Rate:  $15.50 per hour Schedule: Monday–Friday, 7:00 a.m. – 12:00 p.m. During academic year, (may vary based on operational needs). Position Summary Misericordia University is seeking a reliable and customer-focused Campus Shuttle Driver to provide safe and efficient transportation for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. This position supports the daily operations of the University by ensuring dependable shuttle service across campus and designated off-campus locations. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Operate University shuttle vehicles safely and in compliance with all traffic laws and University policies Transport passengers along established routes and schedules Conduct pre- and post-trip vehicle inspections and report any maintenance or safety concerns Maintain a clean and orderly shuttle environment Provide excellent customer service and assist passengers as needed, including individuals with disabilities Maintain accurate logs and required documentation Communicate effectively with supervisors regarding schedule changes, delays, or incidents Adhere to all University safety and risk management guidelines Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent required Valid driver’s license with an acceptable driving record required (CDL preferred but not required, depending on vehicle) Previous driving or customer service experience preferred Strong communication and interpersonal skills Ability to work independently and maintain a consistent schedule Commitment to providing a safe and positive experience for all passengers Must be able to pass a background check and driver record screening Physical Requirements Ability to sit for extended periods while operating a vehicle Ability to assist passengers when needed Ability to work in varying weather 