    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=d687b185-ab48-45f0-afcf-5b1ceb8d32ea&ccId=9200921635429_3&jobId=9200946062788_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct Positions | Chemistry and Biochemistry",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-18\n\nLocation: Dallas\n\nAdjunct Faculty Positions – Chemistry and Biochemistry The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at Misericordia University invites applications for part-time faculty positions to teach undergraduate chemistry lecture and lab courses beginning in fall 2026 semester.  We seek qualified instructors for the following courses: CHM 120 - The Body’s Chemistry in Health and Disease - Introductory Chemistry for Nursing Students CHM 104/104 L - General Chemistry I - General, Organic, and Biochemistry (lecture and laboratory) CHM 133 L - Chemical Principles ( laboratory) Courses may be offered during daytime and/or evening hours and remotely depending on departmental and student needs. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in chemistry, biochemistry or closely related field Demonstrated content knowledge in assigned teaching areas Preferred Qualifications Collegiate teaching experience (lecture and/or lab) Experience with learning management systems (e.g., Blackboard) and technology‑enhanced instruction Instructors for laboratory courses will be required to implement the syllabus, experiments, laboratory activities, assessments, and/or grading standards provided by the Lab Coordinator or Department Chair. Misericordia University is unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa for this position. Candidates must have valid authorization to work in the United States. Misericordia University, a vibrant community founded in 1924 by the Sisters of Mercy! Nestled in the breathtaking Pocono Mountains region of Northeastern Pennsylvania, our campus offers a serene and inspiring backdrop just two hours from the bustling cities of New York and Philadelphia. Here, we celebrate a rich tradition of academic excellence, combining a strong liberal arts foundation with hands-on professional preparation and a commitment to service leadership. Join us in a place where learning and growth flourish in a supportive and inviting environment!",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=d687b185-ab48-45f0-afcf-5b1ceb8d32ea&ccId=9200921635429_3&jobId=9200943179396_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "HVAC Mechanic",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-09\n\nLocation: Dallas\n\nHVAC Mechanic – University Campus Join our campus community and play a vital role in creating a comfortable, safe, and high-performing environment for students, faculty, and staff. As an HVAC Mechanic, you will bring your expertise to support the operation and maintenance of our commercial campus HVAC systems—ensuring our classrooms, residence halls, and facilities remain welcoming spaces for living, learning, and working. Under direct supervision, this position is responsible for operating, maintaining, troubleshooting, and repairing heating, ventilating, and air conditioning systems across campus buildings. Your work will directly contribute to the daily experience of our university community. What You’ll Do: Operate and maintain HVAC systems throughout campus facilities Troubleshoot and repair heating, ventilation, and air conditioning equipment Perform preventative maintenance to optimize system performance and efficiency Help ensure a comfortable and safe environment in academic, residential, and administrative spaces Education: •    Associate's degree/Vocational Diploma in HVAC Technology from an industry leader such as Trane, Carrier, York (minimum 500 hours)  Experience: •    Related experience and/or training in a mechanical or electrical trade.  •    A minimum of 5 years of experience in HVAC maintenance and related equipment •    Experience in chiller maintenance to 500-ton units (screw, centrifugal, and reciprocating types) preferred.  Licenses/Certifications: •    A current and valid PA driver’s license. •    Universal EPA Refrigerant Handling certification. This license number may be used for purchasing refrigerant on behalf of the University for on campus equipment. (Equivalent combinations of education, licenses, certifications and/or experience may be considered.) Why Join Us? Working at a university offers more than just a job, it’s a chance to be part of a mission-driven environment that values growth, collaboration, and community. We offer: Competitive pay and comprehensive benefits package Paid time off and holidays Generous retirement plan options Educational benefits, including tuition assistance A supportive, team-oriented workplace The opportunity to contribute to a vibrant campus environment If you take pride in your craft and want to be part of a team that keeps a university running smoothly, we encourage you to apply.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=d687b185-ab48-45f0-afcf-5b1ceb8d32ea&ccId=9200921635429_3&jobId=9200938960892_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant Women's Lacrosse",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-23\n\nLocation: Dallas\n\nMisericordia University, a member of the NCAA Division III, located in Dallas, PA invites applications for Graduate Assistant Coaching position in Women's Lacrosse. The primary responsibility of the position will be to assist the head coach in all facets of the program, including the recruitment of quality student-athletes, organization and planning of practices, game preparation, administrative duties, scouting and monitoring of student-athlete academic progress. Position may include duties as assigned.  A bachelor's degree is required. Previous participation and/or coaching experience are preferred. These positions include tuition remission, a meal plan and a generous stipend. Misericordia University, celebrated its centennial in 2024 and founded by the Sisters of Mercy, offers baccalaureate, master’s, and doctoral degrees and is located adjacent to the Pocono Mountains region of Northeastern Pennsylvania, approximately 2 hours from New York City and Philadelphia. The university's approach of combining a quality liberal arts education with professional preparation and service to others has resulted in its wide acclaim. .  Misericordia University is unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa for this position. Candidates must have valid authorization to work in the United States.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=d687b185-ab48-45f0-afcf-5b1ceb8d32ea&ccId=9200921635429_3&jobId=9200929201174_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Coordinator | Graduate Education Programs",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-03-26\n\nLocation: Dallas\n\nPosition Overview:  The Coordinator of Graduate Education Programs will report to the Chair of Teacher Education. The coordinator will work in concert with the Director of Graduate Education programs to support, manage, and market Graduate Education programs. Current programs include: MS Education degree programs in Reading, Instructional Technology, and Professional Practice; PDE Endorsement programs in Gifted Education, Integrative STEM Education, Online Instruction and Artificial Intelligence; two continuing professional education programs, ARCH PD and PD OnDemand; and a Reading Specialist certificate program.  Education: A Bachelor’s degree with experience in project/program management in an educational setting is required, however, a Master’s degree in education and PA teacher certification along with public school teaching experience is strongly preferred. Experience: The position requires strong communication, organization, and collaboration skills; fluency in technology applications such as Word, Excel, Google Suites, and survey tools; and an ability to manage multiple ongoing tasks and projects with great attention to detail. The Coordinator must be committed to ensuring student and program success and have a desire for continued professional growth and development.  Licenses/Certifications: Current and valid driver’s license. Work Related Knowledge: A thorough understanding of current state and federal education regulations, initiatives, and trends is required. (Equivalent combinations of education, licenses, certifications and/or experience may be considered.) Misericordia University is unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa for this position. Candidates must have valid authorization to work in the United States.",
