      "title": "Adjunct | Pre-Doctor of Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-03-25\n\nLocation: Dallas\n\nDepartment of Health and Exercise Science / Pre‑Doctor of Physical Therapy Track Position Summary Misericordia University seeks qualified Adjunct Faculty to teach undergraduate courses that support the Pre‑Doctor of Physical Therapy pathway. We invite applications from physical therapists and related professionals who are passionate about preparing students for graduate‑level DPT education and practice. Responsibilities Adjunct faculty may be assigned lecture and/or lab courses in areas such as: Functional Anatomy and Kinesiology Pathophysiology for Rehabilitation Introduction to Physical Therapy and Health Care Systems Biomechanics and Movement Analysis Therapeutic Exercise Principles Neuroscience / Motor Control foundations (introductory level) Evidence‑Based Practice / Introduction to Clinical Research Additional responsibilities include: Designing and delivering courses that build foundational knowledge and clinical reasoning expected for DPT admission Facilitating lab‑based activities such as goniometry, manual muscle testing, posture and gait analysis, and basic therapeutic exercise Integrating professional behaviors, ethics, and interprofessional perspectives into classroom discussions Providing timely, constructive feedback on student performance Maintaining accurate course records and participating in basic departmental communication as needed Minimum Qualifications Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) or master’s degree in Physical Therapy; OR a master’s in Exercise Science, Kinesiology, or related field with significant experience teaching pre‑PT content Current or eligible physical therapy license (preferred for PT‑trained applicants) Strong foundation in human anatomy, kinesiology, and rehabilitation principles Demonstrated ability to communicate complex clinical concepts to undergraduate learners Commitment to the mission and values of Misericordia University Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience at the collegiate level (undergraduate or DPT programs) Active clinical practice in orthopedics, sports, neurology, or related areas Experience mentoring pre‑PT or DPT students in clinical or academic settings Familiarity with CAPTE expectations and pre‑professional preparation for DPT programs Experience with learning management systems and technology‑enhanced teaching Application Materials Required Cover letter describing teaching interests, clinical expertise, and preferred course areas Curriculum vitae or résumé Copy of current PT license (if applicable) Contact information for three references Unofficial transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire) Misericordia University, a vibrant community founded in 1924 by the Sisters of Mercy! Nestled in the breathtaking Pocono Mountains region of Northeastern Pennsylvania, our campus offers a serene and inspiring backdrop just two hours from the bustling cities of New York and Philadelphia. Here, we celebrate a rich tradition of academic excellence, combining a strong liberal arts foundation with hands-on professional preparation and a commitment to service leadership. Join us in a place where learning and growth flourish in a supportive and inviting environment!",
