    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=d687b185-ab48-45f0-afcf-5b1ceb8d32ea&ccId=9200921635429_3&jobId=9200929545429_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct | Pre-Athletic Training",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-03-25\n\nLocation: Dallas\n\nDepartment of Health and Exercise Science / Pre‑Athletic Training Track Position Summary Misericordia University invites applications for Adjunct Faculty to support our Pre‑Athletic Training curriculum on a part‑time, semester‑by‑semester basis. This is an excellent opportunity for certified athletic trainers and related professionals to share their clinical expertise with undergraduate students preparing for entry into professional athletic training programs. Responsibilities Adjunct faculty may be assigned lecture and/or lab courses in areas such as: Introduction to Athletic Training and Sports Medicine Evaluation and Assessment of Athletic Injuries (upper and lower extremity) Therapeutic Modalities Therapeutic Exercise and Rehabilitation Emergency Care and First Aid in Sport Taping, Bracing, and Protective Equipment Clinical Skills / Pre‑AT Practicum seminars Additional responsibilities include: Preparing syllabi, laboratory experiences, and assessment tools aligned with program outcomes and CAATE‑aligned pre‑professional expectations Providing demonstration and supervision of psychomotor skills in a lab/clinical classroom setting Emphasizing evidence‑based practice, documentation, and professional standards of care Providing timely feedback and mentoring to students exploring athletic training as a career Collaborating with program faculty to ensure alignment between didactic coursework and clinical expectations Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in Athletic Training, Exercise Science, Kinesiology, or a closely related field Current certification as a BOC‑certified Athletic Trainer (ATC) Eligible for, or holding, appropriate state licensure for athletic training practice (if applicable) Minimum of 2 years of recent clinical experience as an athletic trainer with physically active populations Strong communication skills and commitment to student‑centered education Preferred Qualifications Collegiate or professional athletics clinical experience Prior experience teaching, precepting, or supervising athletic training students or interns Familiarity with CAATE standards and professional preparation pathways Experience with simulation, skills check‑offs, and competency‑based assessment Experience with learning management systems and basic instructional technology Application Materials Required Cover letter describing clinical background, teaching interests, and availability Curriculum vitae or résumé Copy of current BOC certification and state license (if applicable) Contact information for three professional references Unofficial transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire) Misericordia University, a vibrant community founded in 1924 by the Sisters of Mercy! Nestled in the breathtaking Pocono Mountains region of Northeastern Pennsylvania, our campus offers a serene and inspiring backdrop just two hours from the bustling cities of New York and Philadelphia. Here, we celebrate a rich tradition of academic excellence, combining a strong liberal arts foundation with hands-on professional preparation and a commitment to service leadership. Join us in a place where learning and growth flourish in a supportive and inviting environment!",
