    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=d687b185-ab48-45f0-afcf-5b1ceb8d32ea&ccId=9200921635429_3&jobId=9200929540099_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct | Exercise Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-03-25\n\nLocation: Dallas\n\nDepartment of Health and Exercise Science Position Summary Misericordia University is seeking qualified Adjunct Faculty to teach undergraduate courses in Exercise Science on a part‑time, semester‑by‑semester basis. We welcome dedicated educators who are committed to student learning, professional excellence, and supporting our mission of providing a values‑based education in the Mercy tradition. Responsibilities Adjunct faculty may be assigned lecture or lab courses in areas such as: Exercise Physiology Kinesiology & Biomechanics Strength and Conditioning Anatomy & Physiology (with lab, as appropriate) Motor Behavior / Motor Learning Fitness Assessment & Exercise Prescription Health Promotion & Wellness Additional responsibilities include: Preparing course materials, syllabi, assessments, and lab activities aligned with departmental standards Teaching in face‑to‑face or hybrid modalities, depending on departmental need Providing timely, formative, and summative feedback to students Maintaining accurate academic records, attendance, and grades Supporting an inclusive, student‑centered learning environment Collaborating with program faculty to ensure curricular consistency and accreditation standards Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in Exercise Science, Kinesiology, Exercise Physiology, or a closely related field Demonstrated content knowledge in assigned teaching areas Strong communication and interpersonal skills Commitment to the mission and values of Misericordia University Preferred Qualifications Collegiate teaching experience (lecture and/or lab) Relevant clinical or professional experience in exercise science, fitness, or health‑related fields Professional certifications (e.g., ACSM‑EP, ACSM‑CEP, NSCA‑CSCS, NASM, ACE) Experience with learning management systems (e.g., Blackboard) and technology‑enhanced instruction Experience supervising undergraduate research or applied projects Application Materials Required Cover letter describing teaching interests and availability Curriculum vitae or résumé Contact information for three references Unofficial transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire) Misericordia University, a vibrant community founded in 1924 by the Sisters of Mercy! Nestled in the breathtaking Pocono Mountains region of Northeastern Pennsylvania, our campus offers a serene and inspiring backdrop just two hours from the bustling cities of New York and Philadelphia. Here, we celebrate a rich tradition of academic excellence, combining a strong liberal arts foundation with hands-on professional preparation and a commitment to service leadership. Join us in a place where learning and growth flourish in a supportive and inviting environment!",
